         <td>EMADEB</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,665.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>WOSBAB</td>\n                <td>₦1,800.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,625.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Aradel Targets 2027 for Petrol Production at Ogbele Refinery\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Aradel Holdings Plc plans to begin producing petrol at its Ogbele modular refinery in 2027. The 11,000-barrel-a-day facility in Rivers State currently produces kerosene, diesel, gas oil and naphtha. The company is separately weighing investment in aviation fuel production, which it views as an export opportunity.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/aradel-targets-2027-for-petrol-production-at-ogbele-refinery\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Rise as U.S. Threatens Indefinite Iran Blockage\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude stood at $87.06 per barrel, down marginally by 0.01%, while WTI crude was trading at $81.28 per barrel. Brent and WTI remained on course for weekly gains of about 4%, despite Thursday's decline of more than 2%. The market is being pulled between two competing forces: the threat of prolonged supply disruption in the Middle East and growing concerns over oil demand.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-rise-as-us-threatens-indefinite-iran-blockage\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Crisis Pushes Oil Prices To Tipping Point, $120 Crude in Sight\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The global oil market is showing a widening disconnect between falling crude futures and increasingly tight physical fuel markets. The prolonged disruption to shipping through the Strait of Hormuz continues to erode inventories and restrict supplies. Diesel, gasoil and jet fuel supplies are tightening as refinery disruptions in the Middle East and Russia reduce export availability.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-crisis-pushes-oil-prices-to-tipping-point-120-crude-in-sight\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Refinery May Review Fuel Prices if Market Stays Elevated — Sources\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Dangote Petroleum Refinery may review its petrol and diesel prices upward if current market conditions remain elevated. The potential adjustment would depend largely on whether the elevated market is sustained. Uncertainty surrounding international crude prices and the reopening of the Strait of Hormuz continues to influence pricing expectations across the downstream sector.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-refinery-may-review-fuel-prices-if-market-stays-elevated-sources\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Brent Falls Over 3% to $86 as Oil Prices Extend Decline\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude fell 3.32 percent to $86.03 a barrel by 3:10 p.m. WAT. West Texas Intermediate crude also declined 3.48 percent to £80.37 a barrel. The latest sell-off followed a surprise surge in US commercial crude inventories.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/brent-falls-over-3-to-86-as-oil-prices-extend-decline\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
